{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["In the blessings He placed <b>פְּרִי בִּטְנְךָ</b> (the fruit of your womb) first, and afterward your basket and your kneading-trough (Deuteronomy 28:4–5), for the fruit of the womb is the better and more beloved. But in the curse, He reversed that order, because the punishment reaches him first in his property, and if he does not return, it reaches him in the fruit of his womb. So too in the blessings He placed the defeat of the enemies before the blessing in your storehouses and in all that you undertake (Deuteronomy 28:7–8), for victory over the enemies is for them the glory and the great necessity in the conquest of the lands and in their dwelling securely among the nations. But in the curses He placed the curse in all that you undertake first and afterward the defeat before them (verses 20, 25), for that is the punishment that will reach them last, and so too they will be exiled at the end:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "In the last clause, וְכֵן יִגְלוּ בַּסּוֹף likely anticipates the curse of exile at the end of the chapter; rendered hyper-literally as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:56:19.358765190Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}